   "reason": "C's whole-group transition layer admits DELETE roots: Change::ReserveDelete (DeletePlan) produces the delete Reserve (effect 1, old-row C, planned tombstone projection, DELETE cleanup recipe; ReserveAdopted adopts effect and RowId), DeleteForward/DeleteClr (A's groups) are observed and refused by C's producer as Unsupported, DeletePrune is produced, ReleaseRole steps a delete U; the effect-1 previous root H is proved through entry (b); each leaf step computes the leaf reservation D (typed_leaf refuses entries+D over 16188 as Corrupt, INSERT Reserve/Forward refuse a breaking cell as OrderMismatch); a RowId held by two roots is refused by the after-bank census. RDL-C runs the new independent author tests/fixtures/module-row-format/transition-delete (history H re-run byte-equal to the N1 literals, then history D, 30 groups): 25 C-produced groups byte-equal, 5 A groups observed, 11 variants refused as Corrupt, borrowed observer/producer twins, ReserveAdopted equality, RowId held twice, the effect/opcode rule (INSERT Prune of a delete root, DeletePrune of an INSERT root: IdentityMismatch before output), delete Reserve of the actor's own INSERT row or an absent RowId (IdentityMismatch), leaf reservation bounds for INSERT Reserve (exact fit and one byte short), delete Reserve, A's INSERT Forward (OrderMismatch) and DeletePrune (exact fit taken, inside D Corrupt), and the effect-1 Forward debt binding; the N1 cross-check runs status.rs on effect-1 actors' non-DELETE groups. The effect/opcode, Forward-reservation and replay refusals were each checked by hand to fail with their check removed. The N1/S1A/S1D/S1G literal cases, A's produced groups through C's observers and the recovery Row arm replays pin the INSERT bytes and observations unchanged.",
